From b6a3fb1a4f2dd1aa74bd64c1377b7b0586962e4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:45:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): render authored Bedrock server forms

Render the core-resolved resource-pack form scene through a negotiated
client payload, preserving the original form ID and button indices. Use
accepted pack textures and bundled licensed UI definitions without
starting another asset download when a form opens.

Keep authored control hierarchy, anchors, content dimensions, visibility,
image borders and alpha tracks. Use Java focus, narration and pointer
handling for responses and bounded horizontal or vertical scrolling.
Fall back to the original ordinary form when a visible control, resource
or dimension cannot be rendered, rather than opening an inert menu.

The layout solver and polynomial animation easing remain authored-data
implementations pending full native consumer verification. Keep native
font metrics, asymmetric nine-slice side order, size/UV/color animations
and named next-animation chains as explicit parity boundaries.
